If your intention was to check both conditions separately, you should structure the code differently. Here's an example of how you might want to structure it:

```c
if (x > y) {
    x = 0; // Since x > y, this block executes and sets x to 0
}
if (x == y) {
    y = 0; // This checks if x equals y independently
}
```

